<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Primary Chronicle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1113</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Tale of Bygone Years, Russian Primary Chronicle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Primary Chronicle, or Tale of Bygone Years, is a history of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus</a> from the earliest times to the early 12th century, compiled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> around 1113 and traditionally attributed to the monk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nestor">Nestor</a>. It tells of the Slavic tribes, the calling of the Varangian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rurik">Rurik</a>, Oleg's seizure of Kiev and the conversion under Vladimir. Its oldest surviving copy is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laurentian-codex">Laurentian Codex</a>, written in 1377 for the prince of Nizhny Novgorod-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suzdal">Suzdal</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle.jpg" alt="Primary Chronicle" width="320" height="487" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: from the Middle Ages, unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:14_2_List_of_Radzivill_Chron.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
